SUMMARY:CRH Seminar: FROM INHERITANCE TO INTERVENTION - Reprogramming the Sperm Epigenome
DESCRIPTION:Speaker: Professor Sarah Kimmins (University of Montreal)\nHost: Niamh Forde\n\nProfessor Kimmins holds a Senior Tier 1 Canada Research Chair in the Epigenetic Inheritance of Disease. Her research centers on the molecular basis of epigenetic inheritance, with a particular emphasis on how the paternal environment shapes sperm epigenetic programming, early embryo development, and intergenerational disease risk. She is also Founder and CEO of HisTurn, a male fertility diagnostics company.
LOCATION:IRR SOUTH, SEMINAR ROOM (1.05)
